      "date": "Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:56:51 IST",
      "content": "Home / Education / News / Bihar STET 2026 registration begins for paper 1 & 2; check dates and more Bihar STET 2026 registration begins for paper 1 & 2; check dates and more The Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB) has begun the registration process for the Bihar Secondary Teacher Eligibility Test (STET) 2026 on the official Bihar STET website Bihar STET 2026 apply online Princess Sonika New Delhi 4 min read Last Updated : Aug 18 2026 | 4:07 PM IST Listen to This Article The Bihar Secondary Teacher Eligibility Test (STET) 2026 registration process has begun, according to the Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB). Candidates can apply online via the official STET portal if they want to work as secondary or senior secondary teachers in Bihar. There are two papers in the test. Candidates intending to teach Classes 9 and 10 should use Paper 1, and those wanting to teach Classes 11 and 12 should use Paper 2. Before submitting their applications, candidates should thoroughly review the educational criteria. How to apply for the Bihar STET 2026? · Visit the official Bihar STET website at stetregistration.cbrt.co.in. · Click on the Bihar STET 2026 registration link. · Fill in the required personal and registration details. Also Read IGNOU July 2026 registration last date extended to Aug 31, check details 7 killed, many injured after stampede-like incident in Bihar's Lakhisarai Successful SIR in Bihar led to record turnout in 2025 Assembly polls: CEC GATE 2027 registration date postponed: Check exam schedule, new paper Bihar tops states' fiscal strain with 5.8% fiscal deficit, says Crisil · Log in using the credentials generated during registration. · End the application form with the required academic and other details. · Choose the relevant paper or papers. · Pay the applicable application fee. · Submit the form and check all details carefully. · Download the confirmation page and keep a copy for later use. ALSO READ: IGNOU July 2026 registration last date extended to Aug 31, check details Bihar STET 2026 Eligibility Criteria Applicants must have a B.Ed. and a graduation degree with at least 50% in the relevant topic in order to be eligible for Paper 1.A master's degree in the relevant field and a B.Ed. are required for Paper 2. Additionally, individuals with a B.Ed. in computer science have been granted a separate provision. A 5% relaxation in the required educational qualification is available to candidates who fall into the SC, ST, EBC, BC, and PwBD categories. Before submitting an application, candidates are urged to review the comprehensive notification, especially with regard to subject-specific eligibility conditions. ALSO READ: Delhi Neet protests: SC to form panel to probe police excess allegations Bihar STET 2026 registration fee The number of papers chosen and the candidate's category determine the Bihar STET application fee. When filling out the application, candidates should be careful to choose the appropriate paper and category. The fees for papers 1 and 2 are listed below: · Unreserved, EWS and OBC (₹960)- ₹1,440",
