      "title": "PIB Dehradun to organise regional media workshop 'Vartalaap' in Chamoli on August 20",
      "url": "https://www.indiatimes.com/news/pib-dehradun-to-organize-regional-media-workshop-vartalaap-in-chamoli-on-august-20/articleshow/133322841.html",
      "date": "Wed, 19 Aug 2026 04:15:07 IST",
      "content": "PIB Dehradun to organise regional media workshop 'Vartalaap' in Chamoli on August 20 PIB Dehradun to organise regional media workshop 'Vartalaap' in Chamoli on August 20 Anmol Kumar | Aug 18, 2026, 18:11 IST Share The Press Information Bureau (PIB), Dehradun, will organise a regional media workshop, 'Vartalaap' , in Gopeshwar, Chamoli, on August 20 to strengthen communication between the government and local media. The workshop will focus on disseminating accurate information about Central Government welfare schemes, with special sessions on women and youth empowerment, farmer welfare, healthcare, GI tags, and One District One Product (ODOP). Dehradun: The Press Information Bureau (PIB), Dehradun, under the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting, Government of India, will organise a one-day regional media workshop titled ' Vartalaap ' at the District Panchayat Auditorium in Gopeshwar, Chamoli, on August 20. The programme is aimed at print, electronic, and digital media professionals working in rural and border areas. The workshop seeks to strengthen the bridge between the government's information machinery and local media by providing journalists with authentic, fact-based information on Central Government welfare schemes, policies, and development initiatives. It is designed to ensure that accurate information reaches citizens, particularly in remote and last-mile areas. Organised as part of the Centre's outreach initiatives marking 12 years of public service, good governance, and welfare-focused governance, the workshop will highlight the country's progress in infrastructure and socio-economic development over the past decade. Special sessions will focus on key initiatives related to women’s empowerment, farmer welfare, youth development, healthcare, GI tags, and the One District One Product (ODOP) programme. Participants will also receive information on flagship schemes such as the Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana, Ayushman Bharat–Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana, National Health Mission, Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana, Self-Help Groups, E20 fuel, and the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyan. Experts, senior administrative officials, and experienced journalists will address the workshop and discuss the role of development journalism in creating public awareness. The event will also provide media professionals with an opportunity to interact directly with subject experts and government officials, helping them gain a deeper understanding of government programmes and their impact at the grassroots level. GENERAL Anmol Kumar You may also like 0 Latest Stories Will there be Re:Zero Season 5? Here’s what we know about the anime’s future amid Starting Life in Another World buzz By Iraa Paul Ukraine’s massive drone attack, Lin Shaye’s ‘Insidious’ return & more By Shambhavi Dixit Why does Apoorva Mukhija aka The Rebel Kid no longer live in India? Here’s the reason By Apoorva Mukhija/ IG Why Apoorva Mukhija does not live in India anymore Why is the One Piece manga going on a break after chapter 1191? Here’s what we know By Iraa Paul What if ChatGPT could watch your meetings and read your emails? By Sneha Kumari Mary Kom to join Bigg Boss 20? Here’s the speculation around her entry in Salman Khan’s show By Iraa Paul Bleach: What is Bankai? Second and final upgraded release of a Zanpakutō sword...",
